      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There is a potentially important niche in real-world-asset perpetual markets. Pyth's own reporting cited analysis attributing roughly 96.3% of tracked August RWA-perpetual volume to markets using its data; subsequent quarterly commentary described a share above 94%. Those numbers may signal formidable distribution, but they are not independently established industry-wide market share. They are third-party figures relayed through the project itself, with scope and methodology that deserve scrutiny."
